{
  "raw": {
    "https://une.peopleadmin.com/postings/27112": {
      "title": "Open Rank Biomedical Sciences Faculty",
      "description": "University of New England Career Opportunities | Open Rank Biomedical Sciences Faculty Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Policies Our Colleges Open Rank Biomedical Sciences Faculty Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Type Faculty Faculty Track Tenure-Track Position Title Open Rank Biomedical Sciences Faculty Employment Status Full Time Months 12 Campus Portland, ME Description The Department of Biomedical Sciences at the University of New England College of Osteopathic Medicine invites applications from individuals with a record of innovative biomedical research and interest, experience, and enthusiasm for teaching in an integrated curriculum with a team of biomedical and clinical faculty. Candidates must be enthusiastic about teaching and possess the desire to develop skills in this area. Experience with case-based teaching in a non-lecture format is preferred. The successful hire will advance the missions of the UNE Center for Cell Signaling Research ( CCSR ; https://www.une.edu/research/center-cell-signaling-research ) and COM by developing a strong and collaborative research program in cellular signaling mechanisms or complementary areas relevant to health, disease, and therapeutic innovation. A goal for this position is to have the successful candidate develop the capacity to serve as one of the next generation of Centers of Biomedical Research Excellence ( COBRE ) Research Project Leaders (RPLs). The researcher will contribute to a vibrant interdisciplinary research environment that integrates biomedical discovery with the educational focus of UNE . The successful applicant will be offered a start-up package to establish their research program at the university, including but not limited to laboratory space and reassign time to foster success of research endeavors. Candidates for the tenure-track would have responsibilities in research, teaching, and university/college/departmental services. The successful candidate is expected to develop an independent, novel research program, display a commitment to excellence in teaching by participating in medical student teaching. Continuation of funding is required for this track. Candidates with research interests in a biomedical science topic as it relates to cell signaling, aging, or metabolism, particularly in relation to human disease, are preferred. UNE has strengths in neuroscience, with a collaborative group of neuroscience investigators examining the neurobiology of pain across a variety of pre-clinical models, using sophisticated imaging, molecular, and behavioral analyses. Additional strengths in research include anatomy, cell signaling, metabolic diseases, immunology and infectious diseases, and medical education. Research space is available, with access to shared instrumentation and core facilities with highly-trained staff for comprehensive imaging and histology approaches, behavioral analysis, and in vitro analytical services. Please include the following with your application: a research statement (3 pages) and a teaching statement (1 page). About The University of New England UNE is Maine’s largest private university, with two beautiful coastal campuses in Maine, a one-of-a-kind study-abroad campus in Tangier, Morocco, and an array of flexible online offerings. In an uncommonly welcoming and supportive community, we offer hands-on learning, empowering students to positively impact a world full of challenges. We are the state’s top provider of health professionals and home to Maine’s only medical and dental colleges, a variety of other aligned healthcare programs, and nationally recognized programs in the marine sciences, the natural and social sciences, business, the humanities, and the arts. Benefits Overview Multiple health and dental plan options, plus vision coverage. Up to 8% retirement plan match. Generous leave time, including vacation, sick, and personal time, and 12+ holidays per year. Educational benefits : UNE tuition waiver for employees, spouses, and domestic partners UNE tuition waiver for dependents of employees with 1 year of full-time service. 50% tuition reduction if less than 1 year of full-time service. For more information about our outstanding benefits, please visit: UNE Benefits Overview Responsibilities The candidate’s research program should complement and enhance the diverse biomedical research underway in the CCSR . The CCSR is funded by a phase 1 NIH Centers of Biomedical Research Excellence ( COBRE ) award, and provides research infrastructure, funding, and professional development mentoring for COBRE Research Project Leaders (RPLs) and the larger UNE research community. The candidate will also have the opportunity to take advantage of several competitive internal funding programs supporting new project development. Additional responsibilities include: Participation in team-based delivery of an innovative medical curriculum, and providing academic service to the college, university, and their profession. Facilitate case-based learning. Participate in mentoring and advising activities for medical students. Qualifications Candidates for a position as Assistant Professor should have a doctoral degree and postdoctoral experience, preferably with previous teaching experience. Strong publication record in peer reviewed journals in their research areas. Ability to develop an independent, novel, research program. Excellence in teaching is expected. Demonstrated success in working well with faculty, administrators and students in an educational environment. Strong interpersonal skills. Passion for and commitment to medical student education. EEO Statement Summary Consistent with federal and state law and University policy, the University of New England is committed to the fundamental concept of equal opportunity for all of the members of the University community. The University prohibits, and will not tolerate, discrimination in employment, the provision of academic services or in any other area of University life based on race, color, sex, physical or mental disability, religion, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, ethnicity, genetic information, HIV status, or status as a veteran. Prohibited bias factors should not motivate decisions regarding students, employees, applicants for admission, applicants for employment, contractors, volunteers or participants in and/or users of institutional programs, services, and activities. Vaccination Statement (PLEASE NOTE) Employees in clinical settings must meet the State of Maine’s immunization requirements for clinical activity. Anticipated Pay Range $102,000 - $145,000 commensurate with rank, education, certification, and experience. Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2022F0340P Open Date 10/06/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research Background Optional Documents Names and contact information for three professional references Locations and Contact © 2021 University of New England Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://une.peopleadmin.com/postings/27111": {
      "title": "Open Rank Biomedical Sciences Teaching Faculty",
      "description": "University of New England Career Opportunities | Open Rank Biomedical Sciences Teaching Faculty Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Policies Our Colleges Open Rank Biomedical Sciences Teaching Faculty Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Type Faculty Faculty Track Non Tenure Position Title Open Rank Biomedical Sciences Teaching Faculty Employment Status Full Time Months 12 Campus Portland, ME Description The Department of Biomedical Sciences at the University of New England College of Osteopathic Medicine invites applications from individuals who possess interest, experience, and enthusiasm for teaching in an integrated curriculum with a team of biomedical and clinical faculty, as well as a record of innovative biomedical research. We are looking for individuals with expertise in teaching biochemistry and nutrition to medical students. Candidates must be enthusiastic about teaching and possess the desire to develop skills in this area. Experience with case-based teaching in a non-lecture format is preferred. We are seeking candidates for a Teaching-track position. Candidates for the Teaching-track would primarily have teaching and university/college/departmental service responsibilities, but could engage in research and scholarship. UNE has strengths in neuroscience, with a collaborative group of neuroscience investigators examining the neurobiology of pain across a variety of pre-clinical models, using sophisticated imaging, molecular, and behavioral analyses. Additional strengths in research include anatomy, cell signaling, metabolic diseases, immunology and infectious diseases, and medical education. About The University of New England UNE is Maine’s largest private university, with two beautiful coastal campuses in Maine, a one-of-a-kind study-abroad campus in Tangier, Morocco, and an array of flexible online offerings. In an uncommonly welcoming and supportive community, we offer hands-on learning, empowering students to positively impact a world full of challenges. We are the state’s top provider of health professionals and home to Maine’s only medical and dental colleges, a variety of other interprofessionally aligned health care programs, and nationally recognized programs in the marine sciences, the natural and social sciences, business, the humanities, and the arts. Benefits Overview Multiple health and dental plan options, plus vision coverage. Up to 8% retirement plan match. Generous leave time, including vacation, sick, and personal time, and 12+ holidays per year. Educational benefits : UNE tuition waiver for employees, spouses, and domestic partners. UNE tuition waiver for dependents of employees with 1 year of full-time service. 50% tuition reduction if less than 1 year of full-time service. For more information about our outstanding benefits, please visit: UNE Benefits Overview Responsibilities Team-based delivery of an innovative medical curriculum, and providing academic service to the college, university, and their profession. Facilitate case-based learning. Participate in mentoring and advising activities for medical students. Qualifications Candidates for a position as Assistant Professor should have a doctoral degree and postdoctoral experience, preferably with previous teaching experience. Candidates for advanced positions should also have extensive teaching in the medical education setting with evidence of teaching effectiveness as well as having demonstrated management and leadership capabilities. Demonstrated success in working well with faculty, administrators and students in an educational environment. Knowledge of education pedagogy, assessment, and trends in medical education. Strong interpersonal skills. Passion for and commitment to medical student education. EEO Statement Summary Consistent with federal and state law and University policy, the University of New England is committed to the fundamental concept of equal opportunity for all of the members of the University community. The University prohibits, and will not tolerate, discrimination in employment, the provision of academic services or in any other area of University life based on race, color, sex, physical or mental disability, religion, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, ethnicity, genetic information, HIV status, or status as a veteran. Prohibited bias factors should not motivate decisions regarding students, employees, applicants for admission, applicants for employment, contractors, volunteers or participants in and/or users of institutional programs, services, and activities. Vaccination Statement (PLEASE NOTE) Employees in clinical settings must meet the State of Maine’s immunization requirements for clinical activity. Anticipated Pay Range $102,000 - $145,000 commensurate with rank, education, certification, and experience. Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2022F0339P Open Date 10/06/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Names and contact information for three professional references Locations and Contact © 2021 University of New England Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://une.peopleadmin.com/postings/27110": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Teaching Professor, Biomedical Sciences",
      "description": "University of New England Career Opportunities | Assistant/Associate Teaching Professor, Biomedical Sciences Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Policies Our Colleges Assistant/Associate Teaching Professor, Biomedical Sciences Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Type Faculty Faculty Track Non Tenure Position Title Assistant/Associate Teaching Professor, Biomedical Sciences Employment Status Full Time Months 12 Campus Portland, ME Description The University of New England College of Osteopathic Medicine ( UNE COM ) invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure-track faculty position in the Department of Biomedical Sciences (BMSc). The position includes full benefits, with academic rank commensurate with the candidate’s training and experience. The anticipated FTE distribution is 80% academic and 20% research and/or service. The successful candidate will join a collaborative team of basic scientists, physicians, and staff dedicated to excellence in medical education, scholarly activity, and community service. The faculty member will work across multiple divisions within the Department of Biomedical Sciences and contribute their academic, curricular, service, and/or research expertise to support the department, college, and university missions. About the University of New England UNE is Maine’s largest private university, with two beautiful coastal campuses in Maine, a one-of-a-kind study-abroad campus in Tangier, Morocco, and an array of flexible online offerings. In an uncommonly welcoming and supportive community, we offer hands-on learning, empowering students to positively impact a world full of challenges. We are the state’s top provider of health professionals and home to Maine’s only medical and dental colleges, a variety of other interprofessionally aligned health care programs, and nationally recognized programs in the marine sciences, the natural and social sciences, business, the humanities, and the arts. Benefits Overview Multiple health and dental plan options, plus vision coverage. Up to 8% retirement plan match. Generous leave time, including vacation, sick, and personal time, and 12+ holidays per year. Educational benefits : UNE tuition waiver for employees, spouses, and domestic partners. UNE tuition waiver for dependents of employees with 1 year of full-time service. 50% tuition reduction if less than 1 year of full-time service. For more information about our outstanding benefits, please visit: UNE Benefits Overview Responsibilities Facilitate small groups, provide teaching and perform student assessments in the Osteopathic Clinical Skills course and other areas as assigned; provide teaching for students at UNE’s OPTI and core rotation sites as needed; provide teaching and service at CME programs as assigned. To participate directly in the instruction of osteopathic medical students and graduate students within the college through lecture, small group experiences, laboratory and other settings. Conduct as well as supervise student prosections to be used in the donor lab. To help in planning and implementation of the curriculum and the college’s vision, mission, and strategic plan. To participate in teaching students of other colleges and learners in other programs as assigned. To help with the development of the educational programs of the department and give curricular input to the courses in such a way as to maintain academic standards and quality within the educational programs. To participate in and seek to expand the education offerings of the department to COM , the UNE colleges, and the community in professional and public forums for students, practitioners, and lay persons. To pursue inter-departmental and inter-college cooperation in educational and research programs. To help maintain communication between the department, the administration, and other departments within the college, and other colleges within the university. To participate and serve on committees within the college and the university. To participate in community relations efforts to extend and enhance the visibility and reputation of the Department, the College of Osteopathic Medicine, and the University of New England. To comply with UNE and professional standards and regulations including but not limited to HIPPAA , OSHA , and safety training. To perform related duties as assigned as necessary. Encouraged but not required: To participate in quality educational/academic, clinical, or scientific projects; to help seek external funding for individual research and scholarly needs; to maintain a record of written presentations, publications, and other scholarly activity in recognized scientific journals and books. Qualifications Masters or PhD in anatomy Experience teaching human gross anatomy Preferred 3 years or equivalent of faculty experience in a college of medicine Curricular and teaching experience, in formal and informal teaching, and learner supervision and evaluation Exceptional written and oral communication skills Examples of accomplishments, skills, and publications EEO Statement Summary Consistent with federal and state law and University policy, the University of New England is committed to the fundamental concept of equal opportunity for all of the members of the University community. The University prohibits, and will not tolerate, discrimination in employment, the provision of academic services or in any other area of University life based on race, color, sex, physical or mental disability, religion, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, ethnicity, genetic information, HIV status, or status as a veteran. Prohibited bias factors should not motivate decisions regarding students, employees, applicants for admission, applicants for employment, contractors, volunteers or participants in and/or users of institutional programs, services, and activities. Vaccination Statement (PLEASE NOTE) Employees in clinical settings must meet the State of Maine’s immunization requirements for clinical activity. Anticipated Pay Range $95,000 – $130,000, commensurate with rank, education, certification, and experience. Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2022F0330P Open Date 09/30/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation Names and contact information for three professional references Locations and Contact © 2021 University of New England Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://une.peopleadmin.com/postings/27103": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Clinical Professor",
      "description": "University of New England Career Opportunities | Assistant/Associate Clinical Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Policies Our Colleges Assistant/Associate Clinical Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Type Faculty Faculty Track Clinical Position Title Assistant/Associate Clinical Professor Employment Status Full Time Months 12 Campus Portland, ME Description The University of New England College of Osteopathic Medicine ( COM ) is seeking a full‑time faculty member for a non‑tenure track appointment. This role includes full University benefits and an academic rank aligned with the candidate’s training and experience. As the department’s needs evolve, there will be opportunities to engage in administrative leadership and scholarly activity. Physician Faculty at UNE COM are integral members of their academic department and collaborate across its divisions. Ideal candidates bring experience in academic instruction, curriculum development, clinical practice, patient care, and community engagement. This position joins a team of dedicated physicians and professional staff committed to delivering exceptional education, advancing scholarly work, supporting high‑quality patient care, and contributing meaningfully to the University and surrounding communities. About The University of New England UNE is Maine’s largest private university, with two beautiful coastal campuses in Maine, a one-of-a-kind study-abroad campus in Tangier, Morocco, and an array of flexible online offerings. In an uncommonly welcoming and supportive community, we offer hands-on learning, empowering students to positively impact a world full of challenges. We are the state’s top provider of health professionals and home to Maine’s only medical and dental colleges, a variety of other interprofessionally aligned health care programs, and nationally recognized programs in the marine sciences, the natural and social sciences, business, the humanities, and the arts. Benefits Overview Multiple health and dental plan options, plus vision coverage. Up to 8% retirement plan match. Generous leave time, including vacation, sick, and personal time, and 12+ holidays per year. Educational benefits : UNE tuition waiver for employees, spouses, and domestic partners. UNE tuition waiver for dependents of employees with 1 year of full-time service. 50% tuition reduction if less than 1 year of full-time service. For more information about our outstanding benefits, please visit: UNE Benefits Overview Responsibilities Academics and Teaching: To participate directly in the instruction and development of clinical learning experience in the 4-year continuum of medical student education. To participate directly in the instruction of medical students within the college through lecture, small group experiences (problem and case-based learning), and bedside as time allows. Topics include but are not limited to basic osteopathic manipulative medicine, clinical skills, clinical decision-making (differential diagnosis) and general medical knowledge. To participate in precepting medical students in clinical settings, by giving formal and informal clinical instruction and supervision. To participate in teaching students of other colleges or graduate programs as requested. To participate in graduate medical education as it correlates with the college. To help with the development of the educational programs of the department and give curricular input to the courses in such a way as to maintain academic standards and quality within the educational programs. To help maintain communication between the department, the administration, and other departments within the college, and other colleges within the university. To help the clinical services of the department in such a way as to maintain quality patient care and educational programs for student rotations. Service to the College and University: To participate and serve on committees within the college and the university. To participate in community relations efforts to extend and enhance the visibility and reputation of the Department, the College of Osteopathic Medicine, and the University of New England. To serve on state, regional, and agencies, bureaus, and committees of the profession and specialty or discipline. To comply with UNE and professional standards and regulations including but not limited to HIPAA , OSHA , FERPA and safety training. To perform related duties as assigned as necessary. Qualifications Board Certified DO Physician in Family Medicine or General Internal Medicine; ­comfort with performance and teaching basic skills in Osteopathic Manipulative Medicine is required. Allopathic training will be considered on an individual basis if these skills have been obtained. Specialty Residency Trained to Practice in an area (preferred) Curricular and teaching experience in formal and informal teaching, and learner supervision and evaluation (preferred) Clinical patient care, and clinical team experience Experience in bedside clinical teaching/precepting (preferred) Exceptional written and oral communication skills Outstanding leadership, teaching, and clinical skills Have or be eligible for Maine licensure to practice EEO Statement Summary Consistent with federal and state law and University policy, the University of New England is committed to the fundamental concept of equal opportunity for all of the members of the University community. The University prohibits, and will not tolerate, discrimination in employment, the provision of academic services or in any other area of University life based on race, color, sex, physical or mental disability, religion, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, ethnicity, genetic information, HIV status, or status as a veteran. Prohibited bias factors should not motivate decisions regarding students, employees, applicants for admission, applicants for employment, contractors, volunteers or participants in and/or users of institutional programs, services, and activities. Vaccination Statement (PLEASE NOTE) Employees in clinical settings must meet the State of Maine’s immunization requirements for clinical activity. Anticipated Pay Range $178,000 - $230,000 commensurate with rank, education, certification, and experience.(approved at SRC 09/17) Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2022F0342P Open Date 10/06/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Names and contact information for three professional references Locations and Contact © 2021 University of New England Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://une.peopleadmin.com/postings/27039": {
      "title": "Provost and Senior Vice President of Academic Affairs",
      "description": "University of New England Career Opportunities | Provost and Senior Vice President of Academic Affairs Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Policies Our Colleges Provost and Senior Vice President of Academic Affairs Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Please see Special Instructions for more details. The University of New England has retained the services of Dr. Josh Ward at the executive search firm Korn Ferry. To apply for the position, candidates should submit an up-to-date and detailed curriculum vitae, as well as a brief letter of interest (2-4 pages) describing why you are interested in becoming the next Provost at UNE, why you would be successful based on your professional experience, and why now is a good time for you to consider this opportunity. For priority consideration, please submit all application materials by November 30, 2026. For a copy of the full-length position description, or to submit your curriculum vitae and letter of interest (as separate PDFs), please contact: Josh Ward, PhD Senior Client Partner Higher Education and Academic Medicine Korn Ferry (405) 640-3994 Josh.Ward@KornFerry.com Position Details Position Information Position Type Faculty Faculty Track Tenured Position Title Provost and Senior Vice President of Academic Affairs Employment Status Full Time Months 12 Campus Both ME Campuses Description The University of New England ( UNE ) is seeking a collaborative, visionary, and dynamic Provost and Senior Vice President for Academic Affairs to join a highly innovative university at an exciting time. Reporting to the President, the Provost is the chief academic officer of UNE and is responsible for all aspects of the University’s academic mission. Internally, the Provost provides academic leadership for the University of New England’s two campuses located in Portland, Maine and Biddeford, Maine, and oversees the University’s six colleges (College of Arts and Sciences, the College of Dental Medicine, the Westbrook College of Health Professions, the College of Osteopathic Medicine, the College of Professional Studies, and the College of Business). The deans of the Honors College and the Library also report to the Provost. Externally, the Provost’s Office serves as a communication link with external constituencies, including the Board of Trustees, multiple accrediting agencies, and other key partners. The Provost will be an accomplished scholar who possesses an earned terminal degree and credentials warranting the rank of professor in one of the University’s academic departments. The next Provost will also have an established record of success in academic administration and a visionary leadership style that is engaging and collaborative. The Provost will have exemplary interpersonal emotional intelligence, communication skills, a demonstrated commitment to supporting a multi-campus community, and an appreciation of the national conversations around the opportunities and challenges facing higher education today. Working closely with the President, the Provost plays a key role in developing and implementing UNE’s Strategic Plan, including oversight of scholarship and research activities. The Provost will also build upon the strengths of the colleges, centers of excellence, and other academic units to advance UNE’s reputation for academic excellence, scholarship, and service to the greater community. Working closely with the President and SVP of Finance and Administration, the Provost coordinates the work of all academic units with other offices and operations across the University. The Provost will join UNE during a time of strong undergraduate enrollment and a period of investment optimally positioned for creativity, innovation, and aspirational thinking. The Provost will be a dynamic and entrepreneurial leader with a strong commitment to excellence in higher education, demonstrated administrative skills in leading a complex organization, and the ability to work with a broad array of campus leaders to guide the institution to the next level of distinction. The Provost must have a record demonstrating commitment to maintaining a robust system of shared governance and to advancing transparency and trust across campus. An appreciation for the integral role of UNE in the Portland and Biddeford communities, a willingness to continue developing national and international connections, and, in collaboration with the President, the capacity to attract financial support from the public and private sectors, will be essential. As the chief academic officer of the University to a wide variety of constituencies, the Provost must have an excellent grasp of the challenges and opportunities facing higher education and the ability to connect and collaborate with a variety of stakeholders and groups to achieve collective success. The Provost must also be a decisive leader who embodies integrity, is responsive, collaborative, and creative, and is dedicated to the success and wellbeing of all students. NOMINATIONS AND APPLICATIONS The University of New England has retained the services of Dr. Josh Ward at the executive search firm Korn Ferry. To apply for the position, candidates should submit an up-to-date and detailed curriculum vitae, as well as a brief letter of interest (2-4 pages) describing why you are interested in becoming the next Provost at UNE , why you would be successful based on your professional experience, and why now is a good time for you to consider this opportunity. For priority consideration, please submit all application materials by November 30, 2026. For a copy of the full-length position description, or to submit your curriculum vitae and letter of interest (as separate PDFs), please contact: Josh Ward, PhD Senior Client Partner Higher Education and Academic Medicine Korn Ferry (405) 640-3994 Josh.Ward@KornFerry.com Responsibilities Serves as the chief academic officer of the University Provides vigorous, dynamic leadership, and overall direction for the instructional and research programs of the University Responsible for all aspects of the academic mission Fosters the development of new undergraduate and graduate programs and enhancement of existing academic offerings characterized by UNE’s commitment to integrated experiential, liberal, and professional education Directs all instructional assessment, accreditation, and academic regulatory/compliance initiatives across the University Leads comprehensive student success endeavors with a focus on student recruitment, retention, progression, and graduation Guides research and scholarship activities consistent with an R2 university Promotes an inclusive campus culture that is respectful of human differences Fosters relationships with local, regional, and global partners, thereby expanding networks and opportunities for students, faculty, and professional staff Collaborates in academic space planning and resource allocation Provides leadership and guidance to the University’s various centers and institutes. Serves as liaison between the University Faculty Assembly, the faculty, and the President Collaborates with the President, SVP of Finance and Administration, and other vice presidents to provide leadership in strategic and entrepreneurial planning related to UNE’s mission Works with the President and SVP of Finance and Administration on development and implementation of the University’s academic operating budget Maintains awareness of local, regional, and national trends and developments in higher education Serves for the President in their temporary absence Acts in an advisory role to the President Qualifications Competitive candidates will have a variety of professional experience and personal qualifications, including the following: A doctorate or appropriate terminal degree plus academic credentials that merit an appointment at the rank of Full Professor in one of the University’s colleges is required A leadership style that is built upon empowering others to work towards a shared and collaborative strategic vision balanced with a commitment to execution and implementation Intellectual humility and curiosity balanced with a communication style that projects confidence and diligence Willingness to proactively seek multiple perspectives to collaboratively reach conclusions Ability to effectively navigate, and communicate with, varied stakeholder networks Willingness to become a part of, and invest in, the UNE campus, community, identity, and culture Record of decision-making that prioritizes student-centricity Record of academic and scholarly achievement that demonstrates a commitment to academic excellence Experience as a senior-level administrator with demonstrated leadership skills necessary in managing academic programming and resources to advance the University’s mission and standing Record of success in cultivating consultative relationships between colleges/units for successful, collaborative problem solving Experience creating an inclusive and welcoming climate and environment Knowledge and experience in curriculum design and regional/disciplinary accreditation review and processes Excellence in managerial, interpersonal, and communication Record of success in obtaining external support for scholarly or creative activities with a keen understanding of the broad spectrum of academic research and scholarship Experience and skills in cultivating excellence in scholarship, teaching, and public service as well as an understanding of how these components support UNE’s mission Experience in facilitating strategic planning, assessment of institutional effectiveness, and developing and executing policy and capital improvements to enhance academic programs and implement the University’s strategic plan An approachable and engaging leadership style that fosters connection, community, and a positive campus environment EEO Statement Summary Consistent with federal and state law and University policy, the University of New England is committed to the fundamental concept of equal opportunity for all of the members of the University community. The University prohibits, and will not tolerate, discrimination in employment, the provision of academic services or in any other area of University life based on race, color, sex, physical or mental disability, religion, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, ethnicity, genetic information, HIV status, or status as a veteran. Prohibited bias factors should not motivate decisions regarding students, employees, applicants for admission, applicants for employment, contractors, volunteers or participants in and/or users of institutional programs, services, and activities. Vaccination Statement (PLEASE NOTE) Employees in clinical settings must meet the State of Maine’s immunization requirements for clinical activity. Anticipated Pay Range $325,000 - $375,000 Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2022F0348P Open Date 10/06/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Locations and Contact © 2021 University of New England Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://une.peopleadmin.com/postings/26981": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Entrepreneurship",
      "description": "University of New England Career Opportunities | Assistant/Associate Professor of Entrepreneurship Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Policies Our Colleges Assistant/Associate Professor of Entrepreneurship Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Type Faculty Faculty Track Non Tenure Position Title Assistant/Associate Professor of Entrepreneurship Employment Status Full Time Months 9 Campus Biddeford, ME Description The College of Business (CoB) at the University of New England ( UNE ) invites applications for a full-time, teaching-track Assistant or Associate Professor of Entrepreneurship, beginning August 2027. We are seeking candidates with a doctorate or master’s degree in entrepreneurship, business, or a closely related field ( ABD considered), a strong record of teaching and thought leadership, and experience in applied entrepreneurial or innovation-related engagement, including work in industry, venture development, startups, public scholarship, or with nonprofit and governmental organizations. This position will serve as a cornerstone faculty line for UNE’s entrepreneurship curriculum, which is expanding from its existing Marine Entrepreneurship program to include multiple interdisciplinary pathways. These include new minors in marine and blue economy entrepreneurship and in health and life sciences entrepreneurship, as well as our “Entrepreneurship Across the Curriculum” initiative. The successful candidate will develop and teach undergraduate and graduate courses in entrepreneurship, including introductory and advanced courses across entrepreneurship, innovation, business, management, and related areas. The position carries a 4-4 teaching load (four courses in the Fall semester and four courses in the Spring semester). Furthermore, the successful candidate will also help connect entrepreneurship education to UNE’s strengths in biotechnology, marine sciences, sustainability, and the health professions. The College of Business prioritizes experiential learning, preparing students to apply their knowledge in practical settings. Candidates should demonstrate a commitment to student engagement by creating dynamic, interactive learning experiences that foster critical inquiry, analytical thinking, and active participation. Experience creating or using Open Educational Resources and Open Access software is highly desirable and supports our commitment to zero-cost course materials. This nine-month, teaching-track position offers a competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience, along with opportunities for summer teaching, interdisciplinary collaboration, and career advancement. The successful candidate will join a collegial, engaged faculty in a growing College of Business that is expanding its graduate, professional, and online offerings. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Applications received by November 1, 2026, will receive full consideration. For more information, please visit the CoB website at https://www.une.edu/cob/college-of-business or contact the Chair of the Search Committee, Lisa Herschbach, at lherschbach@une.edu . About The University of New England UNE is Maine’s largest private university, with two beautiful coastal campuses in Maine, a one-of-a-kind study-abroad campus in Tangier, Morocco, and an array of flexible online offerings. In an uncommonly welcoming and supportive community, we offer hands-on learning, empowering students to positively impact a world full of challenges. We are the state’s top provider of health professionals and home to Maine’s only medical and dental colleges, a variety of other aligned health care programs, and nationally recognized programs in the marine sciences, the natural and social sciences, business, the humanities, and the arts. Benefits Overview Multiple health and dental plan options, plus vision coverage. Up to 8% retirement plan match. Generous leave time, including MEPL , sick, and personal time. Educational benefits : UNE tuition waiver for employees, spouses, and domestic partners. UNE tuition waiver for dependents of employees with 1 year of full-time service. 50% tuition reduction if less than 1 year of full-time service. For more information about our outstanding benefits, please visit: UNE Benefits Overview . Responsibilities Teach a 4-4 course load of undergraduate and graduate courses in entrepreneurship, innovation, business, management, and related disciplines. Develop, revise, and assess entrepreneurship curriculum to ensure alignment with industry trends, workforce needs, and program goals. Partner with Entrepreneur-in-Residence staff and external stakeholders to create experiential learning opportunities, including consulting projects, venture development activities, competitions, internships, and startup initiatives. Advise and mentor students pursuing entrepreneurial, innovation, and venture development opportunities. Collaborate with faculty across disciplines to integrate entrepreneurship into programs supporting health professions, biotechnology, marine sciences, sustainability, and related fields. Develop and support programs that strengthen student competencies in innovation, opportunity recognition, business development, entrepreneurial leadership, and problem-solving. Collaborate with College of Business centers to expand entrepreneurship programming, student engagement, and community impact. Establish and maintain partnerships and engagement with entrepreneurs, businesses, investors, nonprofit organizations, and community stakeholders to support student learning and workforce development. Participate in assessment, accreditation, and continuous improvement activities for entrepreneurship programs and courses. Contribute to departmental, college, and university service activities. Qualifications Essential Qualifications Master’s degree in Entrepreneurship, Business, or a closely related field by the time of appointment. Demonstrated teaching, training, mentoring, or professional experience in entrepreneurship, innovation, venture development, business management, or a related field. Ability to teach foundational and advanced entrepreneurship-related coursework. Experience building partnerships with industry, nonprofit, governmental, startup, or entrepreneurial organizations. Strong written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Terminal degree (Ph.D., DBA , or equivalent) in Entrepreneurship, Business, or a related field. Professional experience involving startups, venture development, innovation management, consulting, or entrepreneurial leadership. Experience integrating experiential learning into academic programs. Experience supporting student internships, career readiness, and employer partnerships. EEO Statement Summary Consistent with federal and state law and University policy, the University of New England is committed to the fundamental concept of equal opportunity for all of the members of the University community. The University prohibits, and will not tolerate, discrimination in employment, the provision of academic services or in any other area of University life based on race, color, sex, physical or mental disability, religion, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, ethnicity, genetic information, HIV status, or status as a veteran. Prohibited bias factors should not motivate decisions regarding students, employees, applicants for admission, applicants for employment, contractors, volunteers or participants in and/or users of institutional programs, services, and activities. Vaccination Statement (PLEASE NOTE) Employees in clinical settings must meet the State of Maine’s immunization requirements for clinical activity. Anticipated Pay Range $70,000 - $80,000 Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2022F0344P Open Date 09/25/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Locations and Contact © 2021 University of New England Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://une.peopleadmin.com/postings/26971": {
      "title": "Open Rank Teaching Track, Biomedical Sciences",
      "description": "University of New England Career Opportunities | Open Rank Teaching Track, Biomedical Sciences Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Policies Our Colleges Open Rank Teaching Track, Biomedical Sciences Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Type Faculty Faculty Track Non Tenure Position Title Open Rank Teaching Track, Biomedical Sciences Employment Status Full Time Months 12 Campus Biddeford, ME Description The Department of Biomedical Sciences at the University of New England College of Osteopathic Medicine invites applications from individuals who possess interest, experience, and enthusiasm for teaching in an integrated curriculum with a team of biomedical and clinical faculty, as well as a record of innovative biomedical research. We are looking for individuals with expertise in teaching microbiology to medical students. Candidates must be enthusiastic about teaching and possess the desire to develop skills in this area. Experience with case-based teaching in a non-lecture format is preferred. We are seeking candidates for a Teaching-track position. Candidates for the Teaching-track would primarily have teaching and university/college/departmental services responsibilities, but could engage in research and scholarship. UNE has strengths in neuroscience, with a collaborative group of neuroscience investigators examining the neurobiology of pain across a variety of pre-clinical models, using sophisticated imaging, molecular, and behavioral analyses. Additional strengths in research include anatomy, cell signaling, metabolic diseases, immunology and infectious diseases, and medical education. About the University of New England UNE is Maine’s largest private university, with two beautiful coastal campuses in Maine, a one-of-a-kind study-abroad campus in Tangier, Morocco, and an array of flexible online offerings. In an uncommonly welcoming and supportive community, we offer hands-on learning, empowering students to positively impact a world full of challenges. We are the state’s top provider of health professionals and home to Maine’s only medical and dental colleges, a variety of other interprofessionally aligned health care programs, and nationally recognized programs in the marine sciences, the natural and social sciences, business, the humanities, and the arts. Benefits Overview Multiple health and dental plan options, plus vision coverage. Up to 8% retirement plan match. Generous leave time, including vacation, sick, and personal time, and 12+ holidays per year. Educational benefits : UNE tuition waiver for employees, spouses, and domestic partners. UNE tuition waiver for dependents of employees with 1 year of full-time service. 50% tuition reduction if less than 1 year of full-time service. For more information about our outstanding benefits, please visit: UNE Benefits Overview Responsibilities Responsibilities include team-based delivery of innovative medical curriculum, and providing academic service to the college, university, and his/her profession. Qualifications Candidates should have a doctoral degree, and postdoctoral and teaching experience. EEO Statement Summary Consistent with federal and state law and University policy, the University of New England is committed to the fundamental concept of equal opportunity for all of the members of the University community. The University prohibits, and will not tolerate, discrimination in employment, the provision of academic services or in any other area of University life based on race, color, sex, physical or mental disability, religion, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, ethnicity, genetic information, HIV status, or status as a veteran. Prohibited bias factors should not motivate decisions regarding students, employees, applicants for admission, applicants for employment, contractors, volunteers or participants in and/or users of institutional programs, services, and activities. Vaccination Statement (PLEASE NOTE) Employees in clinical settings must meet the State of Maine’s immunization requirements for clinical activity. Anticipated Pay Range $102,000 - $145,000 commensurate with rank, education, certification, and experience. Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2022F0014P Open Date 09/25/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Scholarly Interests Optional Documents Locations and Contact © 2021 University of New England Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
